  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "<p>Diablo Valley College was founded in 1949 and stands today as one of three publicly supported two-year community colleges in the Contra Costa Community College District. The college has multiple campuses for students to choose from, depending on their preferred location.</p><p>The Pleasant Hill Campus is the primary campus of Diablo Valley College, situated in Pleasant Hill, California. The San Ramon Campus is a satellite campus of Diablo Valley College located in San Ramon, California. Approximately 543 international students from 58 countries take courses at the college each year.</p><h2>What is the Diablo Valley College acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The acceptance rate is 100% for Diablo Valley College.</p> <p>Both college campuses have modern classrooms, computer labs, science laboratories, and specialised facilities for numerous fields of study. The libraries at DVC provide a vast collection of books, research materials, and online resources to aid students in their studies. The campuses also feature art studios, music rooms, and theatre facilities for students to enjoy artistic pursuits. DVC also offers a state-of-the-art fitness centre to promote health and wellness among students. Counselling centres, tutoring centres, career centres, and a student union are all expected resources the college provides with dedication.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p><p>Diablo Valley College is invested in creating an integrative campus where students share ideas and enjoy recreational activities together, thanks in part to the top-notch facilities but also due to the involvement of the student union: Associated Students of Diablo Valley College. There are more than 50 student clubs, including a club for international students. The events held throughout the year include cultural festivals, guest lectures, performances, and sports competitions, where students can choose their level of investment. Students can also get involved with community service to boost their volunteering profile, leadership development programmes and the student government.</p>"
    ],
